 "circuits": [],
 "equations": [],
 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Part numbering",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The base part number carries the suffix -E3 for the RoHS-compliant commercial grade, then a slash and a package code: 54 is 13-inch paper tape and reel of 1400, 73 is ammo pack of 1000. Each unit weighs 1.1 g."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Current rating and lead length",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The 3.0 A average rating holds with 0.5 in (12.5 mm) leads at a lead temperature of 105 °C. Shorter heat-sunk leads allow more current at the same lead temperature; with 0.375 in leads on a PCB, the rating against ambient temperature stays near 3 A to about 70 °C and falls to zero near 170 °C. Junction-to-ambient resistance is 20 °C/W typical on 20 mm x 20 mm copper pads."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Surge",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "A single 8.3 ms half sine of 200 A may be applied on top of rated load. For repeated surge cycles at 60 Hz with the leads at 105 °C, the allowed peak falls to about 120 A at 10 cycles and about 60 A at 100 cycles."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Construction and marking",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Molded epoxy body whose compound is rated UL 94 V-0. Leads are matte tin plated, solderable to J-STD-002 and JESD 22-B102; the E3 finish passes the JESD 201 class 1A whisker test. The body withstands solder dip at 275 °C for at most 10 s (JESD 22-B106). A colour band marks the cathode."
  }
 ],
